2. Study 107: Ifosfamide toxicity in mesenchymal tumors, 74 children, 1yr FU
3. Study 108: Hypertension risk factors in CCS, 1362 cohort, multivariable analysis
4. Study 110: Nephron-sparing surgery vs nephrectomy, 28 children, 40.7mo FU
5. Study 113: Malignant renal tumors retrospective, 77 children, long-term morbidity
6. Study 116: Wilms vs unilateral renal agenesis, 30+17 patients, eGFR comparison
7. Study 120: Oldest adult CCS survivors, 107 patients, nephrectomy-hypertension association
8. Study 131: GST polymorphisms and nephrotoxicity, 42 medulloblastoma patients
9. Study 134: Cisplatin magnesium homeostasis, 22 children, 2.3yr FU
10. Study 138: Renal function up to 5th decade post-URT, 72 children, longitudinal
11. Study 145: Plasma creatinine evolution cisplatin, retrospective, risk factors
12. Study 146: Carboplatin pediatric GCT, 23 patients, 58mo FU
13. Study 150: Renal function recovery post-nephrectomy/NSS, 36 children
14. Study 153: Platinum nephrotoxicity 10yr FU, 63 children, prospective
15. Study 154: NGAL biomarker ifosfamide CRF, 29 children, 4.3yr FU
16. Study 156: Ifosfamide nephrotoxicity pediatric, 20 patients, 16mo FU
17. Study 157: Cisplatin renal follow-up 3+yr, 46 children, comparative
18. Study 159: Antineoplasm treatment GFR, 127 children, cross-sectional
19. Study 161: Progressive glomerular toxicity ifosfamide, 37 children, 29mo FU
