│ "title": "Very late effects of radiotherapy ‐ limiting factor of current radiotherapy techniques", "abstract":       │
│ "BACKGROUND Very late effects of radiotherapy occur within decades after the initial exposure. Their development is  │
│ induced by low doses of ionizing radiation (from 4 Gy per radiation series) and their clinical manifestations are    │
│ difficult to distinguish from other independent diseases diagnosed in individuals not formerly treated with          │
